# Airwallex API Usage

Endpoint reference: `docs/03-airwallex-integration.md` §9. Don't invent endpoints or fields. Verify against https://www.airwallex.com/docs/llms.txt (API pages at `https://www.airwallex.com/docs/api/<product>/<resource>/<action>.md`).

- Go through `src/lib/airwallex/client.ts` only; no raw `fetch` to Airwallex elsewhere.
- Base URL comes from `AIRWALLEX_API_BASE` (sandbox: `https://api.sandbox.airwallex.com`).
- Auth: `POST /api/v1/authentication/login` with `x-client-id` + `x-api-key`. Cache the token and refresh from `expires_at` (minus skew). On 401, re-login once and retry once.
- Acting for a CA (balances, history, payouts): pass `onBehalfOf` → `x-on-behalf-of` header. PaymentIntents use body `connected_account_id` instead (collect-directly model).
- `request_id`: always from `requestIds.ts` builders (for example `fs:{milestoneId}:seller`, max 64 chars). Treat `duplicate_request` as success and retrieve the existing object.
- Amounts: decimal major units (`"90.00"`), converted via `toAwxAmount()`. Never multiply by 100.
- Errors: throw `AirwallexError { status, code, message, traceId }`; callers branch on `code`.
- Every call is logged to `airwallex_logs` with `relatedOfferId`/`relatedMilestoneId` when known. Redact `client_secret` and keys.

Escrow specifics:
- Card rail: create Funds Splits with `auto_release: false` right after PI success. **Never** use `funds_split_data` on PI create (it auto-releases).
- Release: `POST /api/v1/pa/funds_splits/{id}/release`. Refund an unreleased milestone: split reversal, then `pa/refunds/create` with a partial `amount`.
- Wallet rail: `charges/create` (buyer CA → platform) and `connected_account_transfers/create` (platform → CA).
